**Short answer:** Ben Ramsey wrote most of the code that exists today, and losing them would be a real loss. Nobody else comes close.

I ran `git blame` (`-w -M -C`, with `.mailmap` applied) on every file in `src/` and `tests/`. Counts are surviving lines.

**`src/` (about 3,470 lines)**

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Ben Ramsey | 2,171 | 63% |
| Tomasz Wrona | 358 | 10% |
| Carlos C Soto (eclipxe13) | 270 | 8% |
| zf2timo | 223 | 6% |
| icanhazstring | 199 | 6% |
| Kévin Gomez | 145 | 4% |
| Everyone else (about 10 people) | about 100 | 3% |

Wrona's number is misleading. 295 of their 358 lines are the generated `src/Generated/TypeMap.php`. Their hand-written code is `Support/ChunkTrait.php` (51 lines) plus about 12 scattered lines. Without the generated file, Ben's share of `src/` is about 68%. Carlos, Timo and icanhazstring are the real second tier.

**`tests/` (about 3,625 lines)**

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Ben Ramsey | 1,964 | 54% |
| icanhazstring | 594 | 16% |
| Kévin Gomez | 329 | 9% |
| Carlos C Soto | 204 | 6% |
| zf2timo | 174 | 5% |
| Simone Todaro | 113 | 3% |
| peter279k | 91 | 3% |

icanhazstring wrote far more of the tests (594 lines) than of the source (199). Whoever inherits the test suite should know that.

**If Ben leaves**
- Ben wrote the large majority of both source and tests, and nobody else has more than about 10% of `src/` or 16% of `tests/`. Whatever design reasoning lives only in Ben's head goes with them.
- The contributors with real context on the code are Carlos C Soto, icanhazstring, Timo (zf2timo) and Kévin Gomez. Kévin's lines are mostly older code, and I haven't checked whether they're still active.
- Tomasz Wrona is the only recent contributor, with one feature in `ChunkTrait` plus the generated map. The other names are mostly historical.

**Caveats**
- Blame shows who last touched a line, not who designed it. Ben's own bulk commit "Apply new coding standards and static analysis clean-up" (5f4055d) may have taken over lines that others originally wrote. Ben's share is likely a bit inflated.
- 12 `src/` lines are attributed to github-actions (php-cs-fixer). Those aren't real authorship.
- I didn't break ownership down per file, so I can't say which files Ben alone understands. I can run that if you want a list of the riskiest ones for the handover.

