FINAL ANSWER:
## Bus Factor Analysis
Period: all history | Generated: 2026-10-24 | Method: `git blame -w -M -C` on HEAD, so it counts surviving lines. Author identities go through `.mailmap`, which folds Ben's `<email redacted>` into `<email redacted>`. I counted 65 files and about 7,100 lines in `src/` and `tests/`.

### Project-level bus factor: 1
Ben Ramsey alone owns 68% of the surviving lines in `src/` and 54% in `tests/`. That is more than half of the code, so losing Ben leaves more than half of it without a knowledgeable maintainer.

### Who wrote the code today

**`src/`** (3,175 lines, excluding generated code)

| Author | Lines | Share | Files | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Ben Ramsey | 2,171 | 68.4% | 31 | 2026-08 (active) |
| Carlos C Soto | 270 | 8.5% | 12 | 2016 (inactive) |
| zf2timo | 223 | 7.0% | 16 | 2016 (inactive) |
| icanhazstring | 199 | 6.3% | 8 | 2019 (inactive) |
| Kévin Gomez | 145 | 4.6% | 2 | 2018 (inactive) |
| Tomasz Wrona | 63 | 2.0% | 8 | 2026-07 (active) |
| Everyone else | under 1% each | | | |

**`tests/`** (3,625 lines)

| Author | Lines | Share | Files | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Ben Ramsey | 1,964 | 54.2% | 31 | active |
| icanhazstring | 594 | 16.4% | 14 | 2019 |
| Kévin Gomez | 329 | 9.1% | 2 | 2018 |
| Carlos C Soto | 204 | 5.6% | 9 | 2016 |
| zf2timo | 174 | 4.8% | 3 | 2016 |
| Simone Todaro | 113 | 3.1% | 3 | 2020 |
| Everyone else | 2.5% or less each | | | |

Tomasz Wrona is the only other person who has committed recently. Their `.mailmap` entry folds in `T. Wrona`. They own `src/Generated/TypeMap.php` (295 lines, 100%), `src/Support/ChunkTrait.php` and `tests/Support/ChunkTraitTest.php`. All of that is recent work. I listed the generated file separately because it is machine output, not hand-written code.

### Critical risk areas
Ben is the main author (80% or more of surviving lines) of the core public API, with no active second maintainer:

| File | Ben's share | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `src/AbstractArray.php` | 96% | Base class for the collection types |
| `src/ArrayInterface.php` | 94% | |
| `src/Collection.php` | 85% | |
| `src/Map/AbstractMap.php` | 97% | |
| `src/Map/MapInterface.php` | 96% | |
| `src/Map/NamedParameterMap.php` | 95% | |
| `src/DoubleEndedQueueInterface.php` | 80% | |
| `src/Grouping.php` | 98% | |
| `src/Support/TypeTrait.php` | 96% | |
| `tests/types/*` and `tests/stubs/phpstan.php` | 100% | All PHPStan/Psalm type tests |

The type tests are the least-shared area. No one else has ever touched them, so if Ben leaves, nobody else knows the static-analysis contract (generics and templates).

Ben also holds the majority of `AbstractCollection.php` (59%) and `CollectionInterface.php` (71%), which are the central types. I didn't run the dependents count from the skill's Step 3. By structure, though, `AbstractArray`, `AbstractCollection` and `AbstractMap` are the base classes everything else extends, so their dependents are high.

### Areas that aren't Ben-dependent, but whose owners have left
- **Queue and DoubleEndedQueue** (`Queue.php`, `DoubleEndedQueue.php`, and their tests): the main authors are zf2timo (2016) and Kévin Gomez (2018). Ben does not own these, and the original authors are gone. Nobody currently holds this knowledge, so it is a risk even if Ben stays.
- **Set and TypedMap** (`AbstractSet`, `Set`, `Map/TypedMap`, `Map/AbstractTypedMap`, `ValueToStringTrait`): mostly Carlos C Soto (2016), who is also inactive.
- **`ValueExtractorTrait` tests**: mostly icanhazstring (2019), who is also inactive.

### What the loss of Ben would mean
- **Lost knowledge:** the design of the core classes and interfaces, the Map family, the type-test suite, and most of the test suite.
- **Mitigation already present:** Tomasz Wrona is the only recent contributor. They currently own the generated type map and chunking, which are peripheral areas, and are the obvious candidate to bring into the core.
- **Not a gap:** `src/Exception/*` is spread across three or more authors with no one over 67%. It is also trivial code.

### Recommendations
1. **Immediate:** before the handoff, have Ben walk the receiving team through `AbstractArray`, `AbstractCollection`, `Map/AbstractMap` and the `tests/types/` suite. Record the reasoning behind the generics and the PHPStan/Psalm contract in docs.
2. **Short-term:** have the receiving team make a few real changes in the Queue, DoubleEndedQueue and Set code while Ben is still available to review. Those areas have no living expert.
3. **Ongoing:** require two reviewers on interface files (`*Interface.php`) and `tests/types/`. Add a CODEOWNERS entry with at least two names, and consider whether Tomasz Wrona stays involved.

One caveat on the numbers: blame counts surviving lines, so it shows who owns the code today, not who has the most understanding of it. Lines changed by php-cs-fixer or other bulk reformatting go to whoever ran the tool. I used `-w -M -C` to reduce that, but it is not eliminated.

