FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Ben Ramsey wrote about two-thirds of the code that exists today. Most of the rest is from people who left years ago, so the handover has very few people to ask. These are line-level blame figures at HEAD for `src/` and `tests/`, with `.mailmap` applied.

**Who wrote what is in the tree now**

| Author | `src/` | `tests/` | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Ben Ramsey | 66% (2,302 lines, main owner of 22 of 33 files) | 66% (2,381 lines, 25 of 32 files) | Active, last commit 2026-08-05 |
| Tomasz Wrona | 10% (358 lines, 2 files) | 2% | Active, last commit 2026-07-14 |
| Carlos C Soto | 8% | 5.5% | Gone since 2016 |
| icanhazstring | 5% | 13% | Gone since 2019 |
| Kévin Gomez | 4% | 5% | Gone since 2018 |
| zf2timo | 4% | under 1% | Gone since 2016 |
| Simone Todaro | under 1% | 3% | Gone since 2020 |

Everyone else owns 3% or less. That includes David Stockton, peter279k, Tom Carrio and Mohamed Younes, who are all inactive, and Kasia Nowak and the GitHub Actions bot, who are active but own almost nothing.

**What Ben's departure would cost**
- **Bus factor is 2.** Ben has 126 of 253 non-merge commits, about 50%. Only one other contributor (Carlos Soto, 11%) is anywhere close, and Carlos has been gone since 2016.
- **Only one other active person has real code ownership.** Tomasz Wrona is the only other active person with a meaningful share. I haven't checked what his lines are. I'd guess most are in the generated type map, which is 295 lines, but that is an inference.
- **Ben is the only active owner of the core library.** That covers `AbstractCollection`, `CollectionInterface`, `QueueInterface` and `DoubleEndedQueueInterface`. It also covers `ValueExtractorTrait`, `Collection`, `NamedParameterMap` and the exceptions. He holds 69–94% of each, and the rest belongs to inactive authors.
- **`tests/types/` is 100% Ben.** That is the static-analysis type tests.
- **`bin/` is a knowledge silo**, with 3 commits that are all his.
- **Orphaned files get worse.** Today 9 of 33 files in `src/` and 8 of 32 in `tests/` are mostly owned by people who have left. Ben is the main owner of most of the rest, so if he leaves, almost every file in `src/` and `tests/` will be mostly owned by people who have left.

**Files already orphaned**
- **Original Set and typed-map code (Carlos Soto):** `Set`, `AbstractSet`, `Map/TypedMap`, `Map/TypedMapInterface`, `Map/AbstractTypedMap` and `ValueToStringTrait`.
- **Queue code (zf2timo):** `Queue` and `NoSuchElementException`.
- **Deque code (Kévin Gomez):** `DoubleEndedQueue`.

Ben holds 30–46% of each of these, so he is the only person left who knows them.

**Caveats**
- Blame credits whoever last touched a line. The recent "Apply php-cs-fixer changes" and "Bump minimum php" commits may have shifted some lines to Ben that others originally wrote, so his share could be overstated.
- Everyone I'm calling inactive is judged only by whether they have committed in the last 6 months. Some of them may still be reachable.

I'd get Ben to write down the design intent for the orphaned files and the `bin/` scripts before the handover. Pairing someone on the receiving team with Tomasz Wrona would also help.

